  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refugee resettlement to the Republic of Korea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project facilitates refugee resettlement from Thailand to the Republic of Korea (ROK) in 2026 as a durable solution. The project aims to ensure that refugees move and resettle in the Republic of Korea safely and successfully. To achieve this, selected refugees will receive pre-migration health assessments and necessary follow-up care in line with IOM protocols and ROK requirements. Health activities will follow a rights-based approach, safeguarding migrants&apos; dignity and well-being throughout consent procedures, medical examinations, information handling, pre-embarkation checks, and any required treatment or travel health support. Moreover, refugees will be equipped with practical and cultural knowledge to support successful integration. IOM will deliver pre-departure orientation sessions focused on travel preparation and life in the ROK, while also supporting the Government of Korea&apos;s efforts. Additionally, refugees will receive safe and orderly movement assistance, including travel documentation, medical or operational escorts if needed, transportation arrangements, temporary accommodation, and in-transit health support. All activities will be implemented in close coordination with relevant government and international partners.</narrative>
  </description>
